-- @ends-because <reason> is written on a line of its own above a definition
-- whose recursion its author vouches will end, and gives the reason a reader can
-- check. It is an annotation of its own, kept by exactprint and re-emitted by the
-- printer; this file checks that it parses, round-trips, and changes nothing a
-- rule works out.

-- At the top level of a file, above the GIVEN of a definition with inputs.
@ends-because each step moves one day nearer the end date, and the end date is fixed
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`countdown` d MEANS
  IF d EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `countdown` (d MINUS 1)

-- A @desc whose first word is "ends-because" is a description, not the mark.
@desc ends-because in name only
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`described countdown` d MEANS
  IF d EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `described countdown` (d MINUS 1)

§ `Inside a section`

-- In a section, above the GIVEN of a definition.
@ends-because the number of weeks drops by one each time, and a week count cannot be negative
GIVEN w IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`weeks to go` w MEANS
  IF w EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `weeks to go` (w MINUS 1)

-- On a definition in a WHERE: above its GIVEN, at the margin of its block.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sum up to` n MEANS
  `running total` n
  WHERE
    @ends-because the counter drops by one each step and stops at zero
    GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    `running total` k MEANS
      IF k EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE k PLUS `running total` (k MINUS 1)

-- On a definition in a LET, the second of two.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`halvings` n MEANS
  LET
    `twice` m IS m TIMES 2
    @ends-because the number halves each step, and a number below one stops the count
    `steps` m IS IF m < 1 THEN 0 ELSE 1 PLUS `steps` (m DIVIDED BY 2)
  IN `steps` (`twice` n)

#EVAL `countdown` 3
#EVAL `weeks to go` 5
#EVAL `described countdown` 4
#EVAL `sum up to` 4
#EVAL `halvings` 4
